==Strategy==
Elephantidae Papaou is a joke compared to the most obnoxious threat of this level- two '''300% Cadaver Bears''', backed up with a few types of peons, the most notable of which being Sir Rel. You absolutely want to prioritize the Cadaver Bears, so take the [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast Cannon]] and try to kill the Cadaver Bears with it so they cannot revive. [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] is useful for sniping Jackie Pengs or Sir Rels for extra cash, and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] does a lot to Sir Rels.

[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] is incredible here for isolating Elephantidae Papaou; the Zombie threats of the stage will burrow past Doguemon while he tanks Papaou for ages and kills other oncoming peons, making dealing with Cadaver Bears much easier. Bear in mind that Doguemon will likely get shredded once the Sir Rels arrive, however.

Perhaps the most obnoxious part about all this, though? You also need to build your lineup with [[Green Crystal Desert]] in mind, making catering to this stage more difficult.

With the right timing, the default [[Cat Cannon]]/Breakerblast Cannon can be used to prevent a Cadaver Bear from burrowing. Only fire the Cannon every time Cadaver Bear starts to burrow, which prevents it from penetrating your line of defense.

